\ forth/cv8t-numfirst.4 - the gene numfirst for cv8bt.4's byte headers (Iteration 733; results/drafts/esolangs-717.md,
\ numfirst-722.md): a token of digits is converted without its lookup while no name of the form -?[0-9]+ is defined.
\ The flag, NF-FLAG, is the prologue's last padding byte (START + 2 cells - 1: after its two calls, never run), so
\ SAVE-SYSTEM keeps it with the image; HEADER8 sets it when it lays such a name. Two forms: with klookup the engine's
\ (FIND) answers c-addr 0 at once for a token of the form -?[0-9]+ (-DNUMFIRST); without it, INTERPRET8 here skips FIND
\ for one of the form [0-9]+. Loaded into every dump with cv8bt.4, before the dump tool (lab/evolve/evolve.py):
\ tools/layout.py drops the file's words without --numfirst, INTERPRET8 too with --numfirst c; HEADER8 and INTERPRET8
\ then take their places by the X8 rule (this HEADER8 the last, so cv8bt.4's gives way) - the images with the gene off
\ are byte for byte the old ones.
: NUMFIRST-MARK ;   \ where this file's words start, for the converter

: DIGITS? ( c-addr u --- f )
  DUP 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  OVER + SWAP DO I C@ 48 - 10 U< 0= IF UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN LOOP -1 ;

: NF-FLAG ( --- c-addr )   START @ 2 CELLS + 1- ;

: HEADER8 ( --- )
\ cv8bt.4's HEADER8, and the name tested: -?[0-9]+ sets NF-FLAG.
  32 WORD DUP C@ 31 > ABORT" name too long" DUP FIND IF ." Redefining: " HERE COUNT TYPE CR THEN DROP DROP
  HERE COUNT OVER C@ 45 = IF 1- SWAP 1+ SWAP THEN DIGITS? IF 1 NF-FLAG C! THEN
  HERE COUNT CURRENT @ @ HASH 1+ CELLS CURRENT @ + @ HDR-HEAD !
  HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE 4 + HDR-HEAD @ - LINK-LEN ELSE 1 THEN HDR-LEN !
  HERE DUP HDR-LEN @ + HERE C@ 1+ CMOVE>
  HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE HDR-LEN @ + HDR-HEAD @ - ELSE 0 THEN HDR-LEN @ LINK,
  HERE LAST !
  HERE C@ 1+ ALLOT ;

: INTERPRET8 ( ---)
\ kernel.4's INTERPRET, and a token of digits (its first character tested inline) to NUMBER? without FIND while
\ NF-FLAG is clear: NUMBER? and what follows exactly as for a name not found.
  BEGIN
   32 WORD DUP C@
  WHILE
   DUP 1+ C@ 48 - 10 U< IF DUP COUNT DIGITS? NF-FLAG C@ 0= AND ELSE 0 THEN
   IF 0 0 ELSE FIND DUP THEN
   IF
    -1 = STATE @ AND
    IF COMPILE, ELSE EXECUTE ?STACK THEN
   ELSE DROP
    NUMBER? DUP 0= HANDLER @ AND IF -13 THROW THEN 0= ABORT" Undefined word"
    DPL @ 0< IF DROP STATE @ IF POSTPONE LITERAL ELSE ?STACK THEN
    ELSE STATE @ IF SWAP POSTPONE LITERAL POSTPONE LITERAL ELSE ?STACK THEN THEN
   THEN
  REPEAT   DROP
;
